This page is a placeholder colophon, written when the writing section was added.
Edit it, or delete the file. Posts live in `src/lib/posts/`, one `.svx` file each.

## The stack

The site is [SvelteKit](https://svelte.dev/docs/kit) with the static adapter.
Every route is prerendered at build time, so what GitHub Pages serves is plain
HTML: no server, no hydration-dependent content, and link previews work because
the markup is really there.

Content lives in typed files under `src/lib/data/`, not inside components. Adding
a paper or a hackathon win means editing an array; the pages re-render themselves
around it. The one exception is this section: posts are markdown, because prose
does not want to be a data structure.

## Writing a post

Create `src/lib/posts/my-post.svx` with frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: My post
date: 2026-08-06
summary: One sentence for the index page.
tags: ['formal-methods']
draft: true
---
```

`draft: true` keeps it out of the build until you are ready. The filename becomes
the URL. Because `.svx` is markdown *plus* Svelte, a post can import a component
and drop an interactive figure in the middle of a paragraph when it needs one.
